---
// Blog post. Copy authored against briefs/maltipoo-hdb-living.json (2026-07-13).
// Evidence: feeds core HDB page; day-to-day angle
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PawTrail from '../../components/PawTrail.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import AnswerCapsule from '../../components/AnswerCapsule.astro';
import FactsCard from '../../components/FactsCard.astro';
import FAQ from '../../components/FAQ.astro';
import CtaClose from '../../components/CtaClose.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
import { webPageSchema, breadcrumbSchema, faqSchema } from '../../lib/schema';
import featuredImg from '../../assets/site/12-maltipoo-hdb-living-room.webp';

const title = 'Living With a Maltipoo in an HDB Flat | Maltipoo.sg';
const description =
  'The day-to-day of a Maltipoo in an HDB flat: lift and void-deck etiquette, noise courtesy, space setup, and the one-dog rule in practice.';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Blog', url: '/blog' },
  { name: 'HDB Living', url: '/blog/maltipoo-hdb-living' },
];

const faqItems = [
  {
    q: "Do neighbours complain about small dogs?",
    a: "About noise, occasionally; about a quiet dog, essentially never. The barking guide is the insurance policy.",
  },
  {
    q: "Where should the pen go in a small flat?",
    a: "A low-traffic corner with shade and airflow, visible from where the household sits; a velcro dog wants sight-lines, not solitude.",
  },
  {
    q: "Can my Maltipoo use the corridor as a run?",
    a: "No; HDB guidance keeps dogs within the flat, and corridors belong to everyone. Short walks downstairs cover the exercise honestly.",
  },
  {
    q: "Is a balcony safe for a toy dog?",
    a: "With gaps meshed and supervision, as a lounge; never as an unattended run. A 2kg dog and balcony-rail gaps deserve paranoia.",
  },
  {
    q: "How many dogs can I keep in an HDB flat?",
    a: "One dog of an approved breed per flat, and the Maltipoo qualifies by rule 62 as a cross of two approved breeds. A second dog cannot share the same HDB address; that is the rule most owners bump into.",
  },
  {
    q: "How do I keep my Maltipoo quiet for HDB neighbours?",
    a: "Quiet-marker training from week one plus enough daytime company. HDB names continuous barking as the courtesy line, and a trained, un-lonely Maltipoo stays comfortably inside it; the barkers are almost always the dogs left alone all day.",
  },
];

const schemas = [
  webPageSchema({
    path: '/blog/maltipoo-hdb-living',
    title,
    description,
    aboutName: 'Maltipoo HDB flat living',
    datePublished: '2026-07-13',
  }),
  breadcrumbSchema(crumbs),
  faqSchema(faqItems),
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/blog/maltipoo-hdb-living" schemas={schemas}>
  <article>
    <section class="container-site pt-4">
      <div class="rounded-[var(--radius-panel)] bg-tint-200 px-6 py-10 md:px-12 relative overflow-hidden rise-in">
        <div class="absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg class="absolute -top-8 -right-8 w-44 h-44 text-white/40" viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="currentColor"><circle cx="50" cy="50" r="50" /></svg>
          <svg class="absolute top-6 right-[22%] w-9 h-9 text-primary/25 float-soft" style="--float-rot: 14deg" viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="currentColor"><circle cx="16" cy="19" r="9" /><circle cx="8" cy="11" r="3.4" /><circle cx="16" cy="8.5" r="3.4" /><circle cx="24" cy="11" r="3.4" /></svg>
          <svg class="absolute bottom-5 right-[10%] w-7 h-7 text-primary/20 float-soft" style="--float-rot: -10deg; animation-delay: -2.6s" viewBox="0 0 32 32" fill="currentColor"><circle cx="16" cy="19" r="9" /><circle cx="8" cy="11" r="3.4" /><circle cx="16" cy="8.5" r="3.4" /><circle cx="24" cy="11" r="3.4" /></svg>
          <svg class="absolute -bottom-10 -left-10 w-40 h-40 text-primary/8" viewBox="0 0 100 100" fill="currentColor"><circle cx="50" cy="50" r="50" /></svg>
          <div class="absolute bottom-2 left-0 right-0 opacity-30"><PawTrail /></div>
        </div>
        <div class="relative">
        <Breadcrumb items={crumbs} bare class="mb-5" />
        <p class="eyebrow mb-2">Singapore living</p>
        <h1 class="text-[clamp(1.9rem,4vw,2.8rem)] mb-3 max-w-[26ch]">Living with a Maltipoo in an HDB flat</h1>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-soft m-0">By {site.owners}, AVS licensed pet shop owners · Updated 13 July 2026</p>
      </div></div>
    </section>

    <AnswerCapsule question='What is living with a Maltipoo in an HDB flat actually like?'>
      Easy, by design: a 2 to 4kg dog fits any flat layout, needs only short walks, and rides the lift in a carrier or your arms. The real work is social, not spatial: quiet training for corridor noise, considerate lift manners, and remembering the one-dog rule when the second-puppy itch arrives.
    </AnswerCapsule>

    <section class="container-site py-6">
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-[1.6fr_1fr] gap-8 items-start">
        <div class="pop p-6 md:p-8 text-ink-soft space-y-5 max-w-[72ch]">
          <img data-tilt src={featuredImg.src} width={featuredImg.width} height={featuredImg.height} alt="Apricot Maltipoo at home in its playpen corner of an HDB flat" loading="lazy" class="rounded-[var(--radius-media)] w-full h-auto shadow-[var(--shadow-pop)]" />
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink">The space question, retired</h2>
          <p>
            A toy Maltipoo occupies one sofa cushion, one pen corner and whatever lap is available; a 2-room flexi has more room than it needs. The setup that works: pen in a low-traffic corner away from direct afternoon sun, water in every zone the dog uses, and the toilet spot decided before homecoming per the <a href="/blog/maltipoo-potty-training">potty-training guide</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            What flats actually lack is not space but soundproofing, which is why the noise section below is the real HDB chapter.
          </p>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink">Corridor, lift and void-deck manners</h2>
          <p>
            The unwritten rules keep the written ones unnecessary: carry or leash short in lifts (some neighbours are anxious around dogs, and a toy dog underfoot in a crowded lift is at risk anyway), skip the void-deck toilet stops, and give clearance to prayer items and children. A cheerful two-kilogram ambassador converts more dog-skeptical neighbours than any argument.
          </p>
          <p>
            HDB's own guidance asks that dogs stay within the flat and not roam corridors, and names continuous barking as the courtesy line; the <a href="/maltipoo-training">quiet-marker drills</a> are your compliance program.
          </p>
          <h2 class="text-2xl text-ink">The rules, lived rather than recited</h2>
          <p>
            One dog from the approved list per flat is the standing rule, and the full legal picture, including why the Maltipoo qualifies by rule 62, lives in the <a href="/maltipoo-hdb-approved">HDB guide</a>. In practice the rule surfaces exactly twice: at licensing, which we complete with you at purchase, and the day you consider a second dog, which for HDB means it cannot share your address.
          </p>
          <p>
            Renovation seasons, festival fireworks and corridor repainting are the recurring flat-life stress events; the <a href="/blog/maltipoo-crate-training">conditioned pen</a> is the bunker that makes all of them boring.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="md:sticky md:top-24">
        <FactsCard
          heading='HDB living card'
          items={[
            "Space: any flat size works at 2-4kg",
            "Lifts: carry or short-leash, always",
            "Noise: quiet training = neighbour peace",
            "One approved-list dog per flat",
            "Pen corner: shade, water, calm"
          ]}
        />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <FAQ items={faqItems} />

    <CtaClose
      secondaryHeading='The paperwork side'
      secondaryText='Rule 62, licence fees and the one-dog rule, all settled in the HDB guide.'
      secondaryHref='/maltipoo-hdb-approved'
      secondaryLabel='Read the HDB guide'
    />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
